; The XGMII link-partner model — REQ-018's "simulation model owned by DV under
; test/", and the directory tools/check_emitted_verilog.sh looks for when it
; verifies that the XGMII boundary is simulation-only.
;
; Two halves, both DUT-independent:
;   Arrival    the receive-side emitter — SPEC-M03 §8's stress schedule and the
;              requirements.md §0.3 gap arithmetic that produces it
;   Tx_decoder the transmit-side observer — SPEC-M04 §6.1/§9, validating
;              REQ-201 … REQ-206 on a decoded wire
;
; No Hardcaml dependency, on purpose and for the same reason dv_monitors has
; none: the model is exercised on hand-built schedules and word lists, so its
; unit tests fail when the MODEL is wrong rather than when a design is. The
; seam to a live Xgmii port is Xgmii_word.to_wire / of_wire, which a probe
; library will call exactly as test/axi64_probe/ calls Stream_word — that probe
; lands with the first M03 bench, when there is an Xgmii port to attach to.
;
; dv_golden supplies the FCS: REQ-202's verification column requires the wire
; octets to be compared against the independent bit-serial REQ-305 reference
; and warns off a loopback through the design's own engine. dv_monitors is here
; for the octet-time cross-check in test_arrival.ml — the model's own input
; trace, fed to the WO-0012 latency tagger, must show SPEC-M03 §7's front
; offsets of 8 and 12.
;
; libs/** is not depended on and was not opened (PROTOCOL §10).

(library
 (name dv_xgmii)
 (inline_tests)
 (libraries dv_golden dv_monitors)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_expect)))
